 ### Separable Footprint (SF) Projector
-A projector model that accounts for the finite width of detector pixels and volume voxels, providing higher accuracy than methods that do not model finite widths (like Siddon or Joseph), though at higher computational cost [S12, unofficial]. SF models finite detector/voxel widths, whereas Siddon and Joseph do not. SF is more accurate and avoids artifacts produced by Siddon/Joseph in some cases, but is more computationally expensive [S12, unofficial].
